# Citation metadata (Q&A S22-3 (a)). No DOI yet: a Zenodo DOI is planned at the first tag after the
# merge of keck-mosfire into main. Keep `version` equal to keck_etcs.__version__.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use keck_etcs, please cite it with these metadata and quote the code version and the
  calibration release (e.g. mosfire-J-2026.10) that every output reports in meta.keck_etcs_version and
  meta.calib_version.
title: "keck_etcs: exposure time calculators for the Keck spectrographs, grounded in PypeIt reductions"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Prochaska
    given-names: J. Xavier
    affiliation: University of California, Santa Cruz
version: 0.2.5
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/pypeit/keck-etcs"
url: "https://keck-etcs.readthedocs.io"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - exposure time calculator
  - Keck
  - MOSFIRE
  - PypeIt
